  "sourceInstructions": "<root xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-works/ProductModelManuInstructions\">AI-generated fictional demo instructions. Not validated engineering or safety instructions. Head Tube (Product Number HT-8019) part sheet. Fictional shop-floor demonstration for forming Head Tube HT-8019, product 399, from its direct material.<Location LocationID=\"10\" SetupHours=\"0.1\" LaborHours=\"0.3\" MachineHours=\"0.2\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 10 - Frame Forming. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Forming: prepare and form the raw material into an illustrative tube shape.<step>Issue 1.00 EA of <material>Metal Sheet 4 (Product Number MS-2259)</material> and inspect it visually for obvious damage.</step><step>Prepare and form the material into a tubular blank using an <tool>assumed cutting and forming setup</tool>. The sheet-to-tube relationship is illustrated in <diag>2003991</diag>.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"20\" SetupHours=\"0.1\" LaborHours=\"0.2\" MachineHours=\"0.1\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 20 - Frame Welding. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Welding: join the formed blank using an assumed seam-welding process.<step>Hold the formed blank in an <tool>assumed welding fixture</tool> and join its meeting edges; seam placement and weld details are illustrative only.</step><step>Visually check the joined area for obvious discontinuities before transfer.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"30\" SetupHours=\"0.05\" LaborHours=\"0.2\" MachineHours=\"0.0\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 30 - Debur and Polish. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Debur and Polish: remove obvious burrs and perform a simple visual check.<step>Use an <tool>assumed deburring tool</tool> to remove obvious burrs from the tube edges and joined area.</step><step>Visually inspect the tube for damage and remaining sharp edges; set aside any questionable part for review.</step></Location></root>",
